WEBVTT

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:45.060
Miss Mira! Miss Mira!

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.150
"Episode 6
'I'm a Dress-Up Doll!'"
Oh, Mariana?

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.690
"Episode 6
'I'm a Dress-Up Doll!'"
Your food is ready.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.280
I am sorry to put you to this trouble.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.280
Not at all. For you, Miss Mira,
pupil to Master Danblf,

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.290
it's my pleasure to look after you!

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.250
That's a lot of respect there.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.500
Yes!

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:12.630
I do find it relaxing to be up here.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:17.090
It's been a while since I could
take a break. I think I'll take it easy.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:22.430
Even so, my first adventurous trip
in a long time turned out quite nice.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.310
--Safe driving, safe driving.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.930
--I was on my way to see Solomon
after finishing the quest at Nebrapolis.
--Safe driving, safe driving.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:31.730
--I was on my way to see Solomon
after finishing the quest at Nebrapolis.
--Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh!

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.070
Ooh, ooh!

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:38.320
This section has a whole lot more
going on than what really happened.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.320
Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh--

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.910
Garrett! What is it?

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:50.000
W-Well, Miss Mira, a cat suddenly...

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.880
A cat?

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.630
Huh? This is a <i>shikigami</i>.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.970
The familiars that serve diviners, was it?

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.300
Ah, but it's cute...

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.680
Yes, kitty. Kitty!

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:13.270
Um... do you want to do something
to my friend the cat?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:18.030
Or did you come to bully me?

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.440
A wind spirit?!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.030
There's a spirit here?

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.780
Yes. I suppose you cannot see it.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.910
W-W-W-Wait!

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.410
I'm sorry to surprise you.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.540
I mean, this kitty suddenly jumped out,
so we just stopped.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.840
What? Is that so?

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.260
Were you attacked by humans?

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.100
Yes, suddenly on the lakeshore.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.220
In my surprise, I was fleeing
through the grove,

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:53.270
when Nyanmaru drove away the scary people.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.770
Nyanmaru?

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:59.360
Do you know this Nyanmaru's master?

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.700
No, I've never met them before.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.330
Nyanmaru... This taste in names is...

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:11.960
What do you say?

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.080
I am reborn!

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:18.880
I also cleared the quest!

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.340
No, it looks good on you. Really...

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:28.560
So, were you able to talk to Howard
through the Mirror of Darkness?

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.730
No, it seems we didn't
share enough of a bond.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.230
How about Soul Howl?

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:40.980
But there were signs that he was there.
And I also found some likely clues.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:47.370
You... This... Soul Howl is in
for a surprise when he returns.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:52.370
Yes, I brought all the research
materials that he left unattended.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:56.750
It would be most ideal if in
his surprise, he contacts us.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.170
That's true, but...

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.340
So, there you have it, Suleiman.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:05.760
You see, in order to organize and
decipher this esoteric material,

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:09.800
it looks like a lot of knowledge on
spirits and antiquity will be required.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:14.020
You're the only one who
can do such a difficult job.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.600
I'm counting on you.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:19.480
Understood.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.150
Now, then...

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.120
Pardon us!

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:35.160
Welcome back, Miss Mira!
You must be tired from your long trip!

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.790
S-Sure...

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:38.420
For being granted this
opportunity to debut

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:41.590
the masterpiece that
we maids put our all into,

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:44.010
we are truly grateful!

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.010
Huh?!

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:51.600
Solomon! Why you...

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.680
Well then...

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.470
Pardon me!

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:00.980
His Majesty told us of your preferences

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.440
and they have been reflected
in the design of this piece!

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:08.820
I knew that you'd like it.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.200
Right up your alley, right?

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.700
I'm embarrassed to have my tastes exposed!

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.080
This is the robe's user manual.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.630
Well, we will now excuse
ourselves! Withdraw!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.630
Well? How does it feel wearing
a robe made just for you,

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.380
infused with cutting edge technomancy.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:30.720
Technomancy... is that okay?

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.510
It's fine, it's fine!

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:39.270
But you really are as good as ever
at sweet talking people into doing work.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.440
Must be tough to be Suleiman.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:46.530
You really are a little demon.
A little demon...

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:52.030
A-A demon! That's right! I met a demon
at the bottom of the catacombs.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.620
A demon, you say?

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:54.490
Mm.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:07:00.210
A third-ranked count appeared suddenly and
attacked me, so I made mincemeat of him.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:08.300
I actually talked to the guild union
leader in Karanak as well.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.930
The failure of the barrier device
in the ancient temple,

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:14.550
the zombie trouble in Karanak...

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:19.350
On top of that, the appearance
of the third-ranked count demon.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:22.560
Don't you think it all
adds up to something?

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:27.190
However, I don't understand
the objective of the demons.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:28.940
Demons, huh?

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.660
Pardon us!

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.030
They're here again?

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.450
We have brought you tea!

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:42.210
Oh, tea.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.960
Here you go, Miss Mira.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.840
Ah, thank you.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.180
Huh?

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.050
And from there...

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:55.890
Pardon me!

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.600
I knew it!

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:08.610
This time it looks like
your favorite character...

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:11.150
I'm getting goosebumps on my butt.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.790
Oh, I have one more thing I'd like to ask.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:19.830
What is it?

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.910
It seems there've been incidents
where spirits are being attacked.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.540
Do you know anything?

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.080
Even on the way here,

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.840
I met a spirit who was helped
by an independent <i>shikigami</i>.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:30.840
Huh?

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:34.090
That <i>shikigami</i>'s name was Nyanmaru.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:35.300
Nyanmaru?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.590
"Nyanmaru"

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.850
Does that ring a bell?

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.270
If we're talking an expert diviner
with a terrible taste in names,

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.020
who uses <i>shikigami</i>...

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:47.900
One of the Nine Wise Men,
the Elder of the Tower of Divination,

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.860
Kagura of the Seven Stars.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:54.400
I've received reports
about the spirits, too.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.200
It's become clear that there exists
an armed group that's capturing spirits.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.080
Its name is...

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.160
...Chimera Clausen...

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:11.170
It seems that we need
to investigate them more.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.380
Yes.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.220
Pardon us!

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.180
Again!

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:22.720
I'm a dress-up doll!

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:31.190
And you certainly do things
in an awfully roundabout way.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.370
Oh, that's a forbidden area pass.
You went and got one for me.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:43.700
Mm. So, about the Devils' Labyrinth
called Primal Forest,

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:46.080
according to the union leader...

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:49.380
It was deemed a specially
designated forbidden area.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.590
The reason is that the dungeon's
loot keeps respawning,

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.380
and the fighting over it
became intolerable.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.010
It was nominally to prevent this fighting

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.260
that they apparently decided
to seal it as a forbidden area.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:05.730
That's right. On top of that, the only
people who can issue forbidden area passes

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.770
are specially qualified union leaders,

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.400
which makes the process troublesome.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:13.400
Also, that letter with the dates.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:16.360
The one with the strangely
showy signature.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.740
Oh, that.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:20.370
I asked a person named Cyril,

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:24.950
the captain of a guild called
Écarlate Carillon, to investigate.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.580
Cyril?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.960
He's also a player.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.710
I guess a lot happened.

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:36.720
If that's the case,

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.630
I'll contact the union over there
about the demon and stuff,

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.800
and do some spin control.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.520
In the meantime, you should do some
sightseeing in the castle town.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:48.690
Oh, and after that,
why don't you take some time off?

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:51.730
You haven't been on an adventurous
trip in a long time. You must be tired.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.480
You look like that, but you're
actually an old man, after all.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.110
Shut up! Seriously!
What are you saying?! What?!

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.250
This is...

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:15.880
...an enchanted notebook? I was just
thinking that I'd like a secret memo pad.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:19.340
But still, that guy Solomon.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:22.220
Time off? How thoughtful of him.

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.470
Chimera Clausen,

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:29.520
the Devils' Labyrinth
called Primal Forest...

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:33.810
It's a magical communication
from Alcait Castle.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.820
I'll connect you.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.530
This is Suleiman, the Alcait Castle aide.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.820
Ah, Suleiman?

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.870
It's about deciphering the materials
we received the other day...

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:52.000
The work is partially completed,
but a bit of a problem has arisen.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:55.210
Might I ask you to come to Alcait Castle?

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:00.220
Miss Mira has agreed to comply.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:03.390
Then, we'll send a thousand-league
carriage for her immediately.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.680
Well then, I'll be going.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:09.270
Have a safe trip, Miss Mira.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.180
Thanks.

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:11.640
You must work so hard.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:14.940
I have given up on my time off.
See you later.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:25.200
I'm sorry to take up
your precious time off.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:29.080
No, I don't mind. What's the problem?

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:32.210
Suleiman is a scholar and
the think tank of this kingdom

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.750
and even with his knowledge,

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:36.250
he is running into trouble
deciphering this.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:40.090
The Holy Grail of Heavenly Light
that Soul Howl is looking for...

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:43.840
Materials that need to be
procured to make it...

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:49.470
You can get those in the southern part
of the continent... That's broad.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:53.230
Yes, we're having difficulty
pinpointing the exact location.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.850
Having said that, there is one clue,

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:59.230
and I called you because I
wanted you to be in charge of it.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.730
Which is to say?

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.740
"Fool the Wunderkammer."

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:05.410
The depository of a person called
the Crescent Moon Emissary,

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:06.950
which contains all the research
materials and things

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.990
that this person collected
over their lifetime.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.490
It brings back memories.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:15.120
The last time we used it was
when we founded Alcait, was it?

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.580
That's right.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:18.130
I don't mind going,

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:21.630
but remember, the books there
have an anti-removal spell on them.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.720
Not to worry.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:27.220
This paper lets you make a copy
just by pressing it against a page.

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:31.220
Ooh...

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:35.230
The materials to get
are on the third level.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.520
Wait, wait. Didn't that dungeon
only have two floors?

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.190
Maybe it's a result of
this world becoming real.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:44.860
There seem to be a lot more
places we can go to now.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:47.280
Ooh!

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:52.120
And in order to enter the third level,

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.290
you need something
called firefly glowstone

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:56.330
that you can get at
the Lugget Copper Mine.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.250
I'm thinking of sending Garrett
and his subordinates,

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:04.420
but the army is understaffed.
If only we could find a capable escort...

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:05.760
Right?

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.800
Seriously, every time you don't
have enough manpower,

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.800
you immediately start looking at me!

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:12.310
That's something that
hasn't changed one bit!

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:14.850
Really, it's a great help
that you're so perceptive.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:17.810
You're not known as the
One-Man Army for nothing.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.480
Let me borrow

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:24.780
a Dark Knight!

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:27.360
"A bonus
Today's star"
I also summoned that guy
while I was at it!

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.410
It's coming into view!

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:32.450
This is the Lugget Copper Mine!

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.950
That broke me...

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.580
Me, too...

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.340
Was this cat-sith also
summoned by Miss Mira?

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:46.090
Yeah. He's supposed to be
good at searching for things.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:48.380
And the other one is kind of scary...

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.800
It's okay. It's a reassuring armor spirit.

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:53.140
Oh, look!

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.140
"Dig here, meow"

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:55.140
"Dig here, meow"
There, huh?

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:02.650
Is it really here?

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.360
"Believe it's here and it is
Believe it's not and it won't be"

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.360
"Believe it's here and it is
Believe it's not and it won't be"
What's with that cryptic quip?

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:09.070
It should be here!

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:10.780
"Found it?!"

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:12.530
"Found it?!"
Vice Commander, is this it?!

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:13.870
"Found it?!"
Yup, this is.

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:13.950
"Thanks to <i>moi</i>"

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:15.040
"Thanks to <i>moi</i>"
All right!

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:18.910
Okay, let's quickly gather what
we need and get out of here.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:20.420
Yes, sir!

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.290
"Work hard, everyone!"

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:31.220
Okay, that should about do it.
We will now return.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:32.340
Yes, sir!

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.060
"On the way back"

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:41.310
The Dark Knight came all this way with us,
but he had nothing to do in the end.

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:45.150
Having said that, peace is the best...

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.280
Huh?

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.650
A legendary beast?

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.780
"Legendary Beast
Arcus Grage"

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:33.200
The west has finally settled down.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.580
Man, I sure fought like crazy again today.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:47.460
Thanks to that, I'm starving.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.840
The hunger sure is real, isn't it?

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:53.130
What? You get hungry
even from just sitting here?

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.050
Because I'm using my head.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:57.720
Something wrong?

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:01.270
This feeling...

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.070
Listen. You guys take
the firefly glowstone

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.900
and get to the armored jeep!

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.780
I'll draw that thing's attention.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:13.740
No way!

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.990
Vice Commander!

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:16.660
Just go!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.370
Arcus Grage!

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.160
"I'm here, too!!"

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.160
I will be your opponent!

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:34.170
Hey, you wait!

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:43.100
I been looking for this
legendary beast long time!

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.640
I give you loot!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.020
So I want you let me take it down!

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:50.400
P-Please do it.

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.860
Oh, thank you, thank you!

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:00.280
Immortal Arts Skill:
Empty Hands, Empty Mind!

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.540
"Immortal Arts Skill:
Empty Hands, Empty Mind"

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:12.630
Immortal Arts, Movement: Shrinking Earth!

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.800
"Immortal Arts, Movement:
Shrinking Earth"

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:20.050
Immortal arts?
I've seen Miss Mira use those,

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:22.180
but I never knew that
the specialized application

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:24.180
of Shrinking Earth in combat
could be like this!

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:30.610
Not so fast!

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:31.900
Immortal Arts,

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:34.070
Earth: Crimson Bouquet!

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:37.950
"Immortal Arts, Earth:
Crimson Bouquet"

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:50.830
"Bravo"

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:50.830
Hmm, not so tough like I heard.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.500
"Bravo"

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.500
Oh, no, you were a great help.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.840
Hm? What you talk about?

00:18:55.840 --> 00:19:00.720
No, you're right, it was nothing.
That was just wonderful.

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.430
It was no big deal.

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:05.270
More important, I feel
great power in that knight!

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:07.390
What? Knight?

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:10.270
Oh?! When the heck did it get restored?!

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:13.310
Should make much better training
than that legendary beast.

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:15.230
I love fight match together.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:19.650
Oh, um... This knight is here
with us as our escort,

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:22.490
so it can't accept that kind of matchup.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:23.990
I'm very sorry about that.

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.910
Crushed!

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:32.750
So, you not the mage.
Can't be helped then.

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:36.670
So she knows full well that
the Dark Knight was summoned.

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:40.720
If you really wish it, I believe
you should go to Lunatic Lake.

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:42.550
Lunatic Lake?

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:47.470
Yes, the person who summoned
this Dark Knight is there.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:50.270
Lunatic Lake...

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.770
Too early to return!

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:58.070
Some other time!

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.200
Who the heck was that...?

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.070
The mission is complete, meow!

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.530
Yeah.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.120
What?!

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:10.370
You can speak?!

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.210
Ah, I feel so much better.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.750
So? You peed?

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:18.090
I peed.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:21.930
It's been 30 years since we've
had this exchange, but I mean...

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.930
That conversation with you
looking like that? Just no.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.310
We have completed the mission.

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:32.350
Ah...

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:36.560
Miss Mira, thank you for lending
the Dark Knight to us.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:39.070
Oh, it's not even worth mentioning.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:43.360
More importantly, the Dark Knight
seems to be at a heightened alert level.

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:45.200
What happened?

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.950
Well, it was attacked
by a legendary beast,

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.910
and then saved by a girl
using Immortal Arts.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:51.370
What kind of girl?

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.960
She had hair like this

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:56.460
and spoke oddly, like, "I do it!"

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:58.000
Oh.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.500
You know her?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.210
Maybe.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:05.510
Well, for more information,
we'll check the report later.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:07.180
You may go.

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:09.510
Yes, please pardon me.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:13.180
So, what do you think?

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:16.480
Ten to one that's probably Meilin.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:17.940
Yeah!

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:21.360
She may be on one of her
usual training journeys,

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:24.360
but if she's in the area,
she could at least drop by.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:28.200
It can't be helped. When you're saddled
with being one of the Nine Wise Men,

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:31.660
if you come back, you get
run ragged by this guy.

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:37.830
You can't even casually go off
on a training trip. Like me.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:41.380
If we wait, do you suppose she'll
eventually return out of the blue?

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.170
Hmm, I don't know about that.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:46.510
She was the type to forget promises
if she got engrossed in something.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:49.890
If only we had some more
proper people of character.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:51.390
Yeah.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:56.270
Seriously! All of them
just running about out there.

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:58.440
I wish they'd think of the trouble
it takes me to find them.

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:01.900
I know, right? When it's just me,
I'm too busy for words.

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:03.860
It's like, show some consideration there.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:04.900
No kidding!

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:08.700
--Well, let's put this matter on hold.
--Lately, lots of demons keep appearing,
so there's no break.

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:10.740
Now, then, the firefly glowstones

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:15.290
are effective for a
limited amount of time.

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:18.170
So, what say we get going!
